    <bpmn:process id="W_W1198" name="W1198. Installation Material Kit Pre-Stage, Quality Check &amp; Site-Ready Packing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Installation service order confirmed with scheduled date (W138 Step 4)
Frequency: ~500–800 installation orders/week chain-wide; ~3–4 per store per week
Volume: Each installation kit contains 5–25 line items depending on installation type
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Stock Associate, Receiving Clerk, Installation Contractor, Customer Service Rep
Source: workflow W1198 — Installation Material Kit Pre-Stage, Quality Check &amp; Site-Ready Packing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1198_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1198_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1198_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1198_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1198_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1198_Start5" name="Installation service order confirmed with scheduled date (W138 Step 4)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1198_Task6" name="Kit pull list generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Kit pull list generation: 24 hours before scheduled installation: system generates &quot;Installation Kit Pull List&quot; from the service order (W138); pull list includes: (a) primary product (AC unit, water heater, tiles, toilet), (b) ancillary materials (adhesive, grout, copper pipes, electrical wire, brackets, screws, sealant), (c) consumables (drill bits, blades, tape — included in installation fee); pull list sent to Stock Associate&#x27;s handheld device
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1198_Task7" name="Material picking and staging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material picking and staging: Stock Associate picks all items per pull list from store inventory; stages in designated &quot;Installation Staging Area&quot; in backroom; scans each item barcode to confirm pick; flags any out-of-stock items immediately: (a) Stock Associate checks alternate store availability for same-day transfer, (b) if unavailable: notifies CSR to contact customer for reschedule or substitution approval
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1198_Task8" name="Quality verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quality verification: Receiving Clerk performs quality check on picked items: (a) primary product: verify correct model, color, size, and undamaged packaging, (b) tiles: verify correct batch/shade number (consistency per W421), (c) paint: verify correct tint formula if custom color, (d) fragile items: verify no cracks, chips, or dents, (e) electrical items: verify correct specifications (voltage, wattage, amperage); rejects any damaged or incorrect items for replacement
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1198_Task9" name="Site-ready packing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Site-ready packing: Stock Associate packs verified items for transport to customer site: (a) fragile items (tiles, sanitary ware) wrapped in bubble wrap and packed vertically in crate, (b) heavy items (AC outdoor unit, water heater) secured on dolly, (c) small parts and fittings in labeled zip-lock bags grouped by installation step, (d) installation checklist and warranty card attached to outside of kit, (e) &quot;Installation Kit — [Customer Name] — [Date]&quot; label applied
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–20 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1198_Task10" name="Contractor handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contractor handoff: Installation contractor arrives at store on scheduled day; Stock Associate presents staged kit; contractor reviews pull list against physical items; confirms completeness by signing digital handoff form; contractor loads materials into vehicle
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Contractor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min/handoff</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1198_Task11" name="Post-installation unused materials return">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-installation unused materials return: After installation, contractor returns any unused materials to store with installation completion report; Receiving Clerk receives returns; system reverses inventory issuance for returned items; adjusts service order cost for actual materials consumed
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Contractor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min/return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1198_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1198_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1198_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1198_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-275 (ensure controlled execution — Installation &amp; Repair Services (PA-12.1).) | - operational: 24-hour pre-stage in Step 1 and immediate escalation for substitutions in Step 2; operational: batch verification in Step 3 per W421; operational: 4-hour pickup window after which kit is destaged and materials returned to shelf
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1198_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1198_Annotation13" targetRef="W1198_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow15" sourceRef="W1198_Start5" targetRef="W1198_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow16" sourceRef="W1198_Task6" targetRef="W1198_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow17" sourceRef="W1198_Task7" targetRef="W1198_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow18" sourceRef="W1198_Task8" targetRef="W1198_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow19" sourceRef="W1198_Task9" targetRef="W1198_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow20" sourceRef="W1198_Task10" targetRef="W1198_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1198_Flow21" sourceRef="W1198_Task11" targetRef="W1198_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
