    <bpmn:process id="W_W1171" name="W1171. Installation Defect Punch List, Customer Walk-Through &amp; Quality Sign-Off" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Subcontractor completes installation work order (W1170) and reports &quot;Installation Complete&quot;
Frequency: ~500–800 installations/week chain-wide
Volume: Every installation requires quality sign-off; ~5–10% require punch list defect remediation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Store) / Services Quality Inspector
Participants: Subcontractor, Customer, Department Supervisor, Services Quality Inspector (HQ), Services Manager
Source: workflow W1171 — Installation Defect Punch List, Customer Walk-Through &amp; Quality Sign-Off</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1171_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1171_Lane1" name="Subcontractor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1171_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1171_Lane3" name="Services Quality Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1171_Lane4" name="Services Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1171_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1171_Start6" name="Subcontractor completes installation work order (W1170) and reports &quot;Installation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1171_Task7" name="Completion notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Completion notification: Subcontractor marks work order &quot;Installation Complete&quot; in mobile app; uploads photos of finished installation from multiple angles; system notifies Department Supervisor and customer
Responsible (R): Subcontractor / System
Accountable (A): Services Dispatch Coordinator
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1171_Task8" name="Customer walk-through">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer walk-through: Subcontractor conducts in-person walk-through with customer: (a) demonstrate installed product functionality (e.g., AC cooling test, water heater flow test, tile alignment check); (b) explain warranty terms and maintenance per W821; (c) present digital punch list form on tablet for customer review; (d) customer notes any defects, incomplete work, or cosmetic issues
Responsible (R): Subcontractor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1171_Task9" name="Quality checklist completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quality checklist completion: Subcontractor completes digital quality checklist per service type: (a) AC installation: mounting stability, refrigerant line connections, drain pipe slope, electrical connection, thermostat calibration; (b) tile installation: grout line consistency, surface flatness (no lippage &gt; 1mm), waterproofing membrane integrity, slope to drain; (c) water heater: pipe connections leak-free, temperature-pressure relief valve functional, electrical grounding; (d) each checklist item rated Pass/Fail/Minor Defect; photos required for each category
Responsible (R): Subcontractor
Accountable (A): Services Quality Inspector
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1171_Task10" name="Defect documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Defect documentation: If customer identifies defects or checklist items fail: (a) system creates Punch List with defect descriptions, photos, and severity (Critical: safety or functional failure; Major: visible cosmetic or performance issue; Minor: cosmetic imperfection); (b) Critical defects: subcontractor must remediate same day; (c) Major defects: remediation within 48 hours; (d) Minor defects: remediation within 7 days or customer may accept as-is with sign-off; (e) system schedules remediation visit per W1170 dispatch
Responsible (R): Subcontractor / System
Accountable (A): Services Quality Inspector
Duration: 10 min/defect</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1171_Task11" name="Customer sign-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer sign-off: If walk-through is satisfactory (no defects or only minor accepted): (a) customer signs digital acceptance form on tablet; (b) system updates work order status to &quot;Accepted&quot;; (c) triggers service revenue recognition per W16; (d) triggers subcontractor payment processing per W600 agreement (payment within 15 days of acceptance); (e) system enrolls project in warranty tracking per W821
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1171_Task12" name="Post-acceptance quality audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-acceptance quality audit: Services Quality Inspector conducts random post-acceptance audit on 10% of installations: (a) visit customer site within 7 days of sign-off; (b) independently verify quality checklist items; (c) interview customer on satisfaction; (d) compare audit findings to subcontractor&#x27;s self-reported checklist; (e) discrepancy rate feeds subcontractor scorecard per W213 and W600
Responsible (R): Services Quality Inspector
Accountable (A): Services Manager
Duration: 45–60 min/audit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1171_Task13" name="Monthly quality analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly quality analytics: Services Manager compiles installation quality dashboard: (a) first-time fix rate (installations accepted without punch list), (b) punch list defect rate by type and subcontractor, (c) customer satisfaction score by service type, (d) post-acceptance audit discrepancy rate, (e) remediation cycle time; identify underperforming subcontractors for corrective action per W213
Responsible (R): Services Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1171_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1171_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1171_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1171_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-186 (ensure installation quality &amp; warranty registration.) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Store) / Services Quality Inspector review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Store) / Services Quality Inspector</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1171_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1171_Annotation15" targetRef="W1171_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1171_Flow17" sourceRef="W1171_Start6" targetRef="W1171_Task7" />
