    <bpmn:process id="W_W1520" name="W1520. Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Installation Service Measurement, Layout Planning &amp; Waste Factor Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases tiles, vinyl planks, or laminate flooring and requests installation service
Frequency: ~200–350 tile/flooring installation orders/month chain-wide
Volume: Average material value: PHP 15,000–80,000; installation labor: PHP 5,000–25,000
Owner: Service Coordinator
Participants: Service Coordinator, Tile Installation Subcontractor, Project Estimator, Customer
Source: workflow W1520 — Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Installation Service Measurement, Layout Planning &amp; Waste Factor Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1520_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1520_Lane1" name="Service Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1520_Lane2" name="Tile Subcontractor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1520_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1520_Start4" name="Customer purchases tiles, vinyl planks, or laminate flooring and requests installation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task5" name="Service order creation and measurement review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Service order creation and measurement review: (a) at POS or service counter: customer selects tiles/flooring + installation service SKU; (b) Service Coordinator reviews measurement data: (i) if customer used in-store estimation service (W963, W1061): pull area calculations, tile quantity, grout, adhesive, and recommended waste factor from estimation record; (ii) if no prior estimation: schedule site measurement visit (W442) to get accurate room dimensions; (c) Service Coordinator creates service order with: installation type (ceramic tile, porcelain tile, vinyl plank, laminate), area (sqm), substrate condition (concrete, existing tile, wood), pattern complexity (straight lay, diagonal, herringbone), and preferred schedule
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task6" name="Site measurement and substrate assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Site measurement and substrate assessment (mandatory for tile, optional for vinyl/laminate): (a) subcontractor visits site and measures: (i) precise room dimensions (length × width of each area), (ii) identifies obstacles (toilet flange, doorways, columns, built-in cabinets), (iii) checks substrate condition: (a) concrete substrate: level? cracks? moisture? curing age (&gt;28 days required), (b) existing tile: can install over or must remove?, (c) wood substrate: structural integrity, deflection test; (b) subcontractor documents with photos and videos; (c) updates quantity estimate in system: actual sqm vs. planned sqm, waste factor recommendation (10% straight lay, 15% diagonal/herringbone, 20% for rooms with many cuts/obstacles)
Responsible (R): Tile Subcontractor
Accountable (A): Service Coordinator
Duration: 30–60 min/site visit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task7" name="Material confirmation and waste factor communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material confirmation and waste factor communication: (a) Service Coordinator reviews site assessment; (b) presents updated material quantity to customer: (i) base quantity (actual sqm ÷ tile sqm/pc), (ii) waste factor (10–20% based on pattern and complexity), (iii) total order quantity; (c) explains waste factor necessity: &quot;tiles break during cutting, rooms are never perfectly square, you need spare tiles for future repairs — this batch color may not be available later&quot;; (d) customer confirms final material order + any additional materials (tile adhesive, grout, spacers, waterproofing membrane for wet areas, transition strips, baseboard); (e) system adjusts sales order if additional tiles/materials needed
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task8" name="Installation scheduling and dispatch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Installation scheduling and dispatch: (a) Service Coordinator assigns to accredited tile setter subcontractor; (b) schedules installation (tile installation typically requires 2–5 days depending on area and complexity: Day 1 substrate prep + waterproofing, Day 2–3 tile laying, Day 4 grouting, Day 5 cleanup); (c) ensures all materials delivered to site or available at store for pickup before installation start
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task9" name="Installation execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Installation execution: (a) subcontractor arrives at site; verifies all materials present and correct batch/shade; (b) performs installation: (i) substrate preparation: clean, level, apply waterproofing membrane (for wet areas — bathroom, kitchen), (ii) layout planning: establish center lines, check pattern alignment with doorways, dry-lay key areas to verify pattern; (iii) tile laying: apply adhesive with notched trowel, set tiles with spacers, check level every 3–4 tiles, cut tiles for edges and obstacles with wet saw; (iv) grouting: after adhesive cures (24 hours), apply grout, clean excess, seal grout lines; (v) final cleanup: remove spacers, clean tile surface, install transition strips and baseboard; (c) captures progress photos at each stage via mobile app
Responsible (R): Tile Subcontractor
Accountable (A): Service Coordinator
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task10" name="Quality inspection and sign-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quality inspection and sign-off: (a) subcontractor performs self-inspection: grout line consistency, lippage check (max 1mm for rectified tile, 2mm for standard tile), hollow-sounding tile check (tap test every tile — hollow indicates poor adhesive contact), slope check in wet areas (water should flow toward drain); (b) customer inspects completed installation; (c) customer signs digital completion certificate per W1254; (d) system registers 12-month installation warranty; (e) subcontractor marks job complete
Responsible (R): Tile Subcontractor / Customer
Accountable (A): Service Coordinator
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1520_Task11" name="Post-grout curing follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-grout curing follow-up (24–48 hours after completion): (a) Service Coordinator contacts customer to confirm satisfaction after grout has fully cured and customer has had time to inspect under natural light; (b) addresses any concerns (hollow tiles, grout cracks, uneven areas); (c) if issues found: dispatch subcontractor for remediation per W795; (d) if satisfied: service order formally closed
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1520_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1520_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1520_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1520_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-275 (ensure controlled execution — Installation &amp; Repair Services (PA-12.1).) | - operational: strong waste factor communication but customer resistance persists
Owner: Service Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1520_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1520_Annotation13" targetRef="W1520_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow15" sourceRef="W1520_Start4" targetRef="W1520_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow16" sourceRef="W1520_Task5" targetRef="W1520_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow17" sourceRef="W1520_Task6" targetRef="W1520_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow18" sourceRef="W1520_Task7" targetRef="W1520_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow19" sourceRef="W1520_Task8" targetRef="W1520_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow20" sourceRef="W1520_Task9" targetRef="W1520_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow21" sourceRef="W1520_Task10" targetRef="W1520_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1520_Flow22" sourceRef="W1520_Task11" targetRef="W1520_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1520_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1520_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1520">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1520_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1520_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1520_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1520_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
